### v1.0.4 — Core Infrastructure

- [x] Single-pass atomic alias LDAP query replacing legacy iterative loops (reduces export time from 30+ min to seconds on large installations) (v1.0.4)
- [x] Universal LDAP URI resolver fallback via `zmlocalconfig`, `ldap_url`, and `ldap_master_url` (v1.0.4)
- [x] Anchored regex mailbox account filtering preventing false exclusions on legitimate usernames (v1.0.4)
- [x] Portable in-place file replacement `portable_replace()` for cross-platform GNU/BSD compatibility (v1.0.4)
- [x] Progress-aware timestamped batch mailbox export and import script generation with error tracking counters (v1.0.4)
- [x] Mailbox size reporting utility `util/mailbox_size.sh` with dynamic unit scaling (Bytes/KB/MB/GB/TB) (v1.0.4)
- [x] Email forwarding audit utility `util/audit_forwards.sh` covering both admin and webmail forwarding rules (v1.0.4)
- [x] Shared folders and calendar permissions audit utility `util/audit_shares.sh` (v1.0.4)
- [x] Domain disclaimer injection utility `util/add_disclaimer.sh` per-domain via `zimbraAmavisDomainDisclaimerText` (v1.0.4)
- [x] Dedicated session audit logging with timestamped log files per export session (v1.0.4)
- [x] Automated domain export via `DOMINIOS.ldif` and companion script `create_domains.sh` for target provisioning (v1.0.4)
- [x] Flexible mailbox export filters: all accounts, active-only, or per-domain (v1.0.4)
- [x] Global MTA configuration snapshot `CONFIG_GLOBAL.ldif` and `global_settings_snapshot.txt` (v1.0.4)
- [x] Immediate live mailbox export trigger option from within `z2z.sh` session (v1.0.4)

### v1.0.5 — Extended Migration Coverage + Codebase Audit

- [x] Export and restore user webmail signatures and persona identities via `zmprov gsig/csig/gid/mid` with plain-text and HTML variant support (`util/export_signatures.sh`, `util/import_signatures.sh`) (v1.0.5)
- [x] Export and restore user Sieve mail filter rules from `zimbraMailSieveScript` LDAP attribute with safe in-memory handling (`util/export_sieve_filters.sh`, `util/import_sieve_filters.sh`) (v1.0.5)
- [x] Export and restore Out-of-Office vacation auto-reply status, message body, and date range with `YYYYMMDDHHMMSSZ` format validation (`util/export_ooo.sh`, `util/import_ooo.sh`) (v1.0.5)
- [x] Export and provision calendar resources and equipment accounts (`zimbraCalResType`) including calendar TGZ data migration (`util/export_calendar_resources.sh`, `util/import_calendar_resources.sh`) (v1.0.5)
- [x] Pre-flight DNS diagnostic utility validating domain MX, SPF, DKIM, and DMARC records with local resolver reachability check (`util/dns_diagnostic.sh`) (v1.0.5)
- [x] DKIM key snapshot utility with regeneration advisory for secure key rotation on the destination server (`util/export_dkim_keys.sh`) (v1.0.5)

### v1.0.5 — Bug Fixes & Hardening (Maintenance Pass)

- [x] Fixed critical `set -e` arithmetic abort: all `((var++))` increments now use `|| true` across `func.sh`, all `util/` scripts, and generated batch scripts (v1.0.5)
- [x] Fixed infinite recursion / stack overflow risk in 8 interactive prompt functions across `func.sh` and `skell/importar_ldap.sh` — converted to `while true` loops (v1.0.5)
- [x] Fixed `portable_replace()` temp file leak and file corruption risk on `sed` failure — added `if/else` with `rm -f` on all failure paths (v1.0.5)
- [x] Fixed `export_sieve_filters.sh` trap race condition — replaced per-iteration `trap`/`trap -` with single global cleanup function (v1.0.5)
- [x] Fixed `export_calendar_resources.sh` FAILED counter never incremented — failure branch now correctly increments `FAILED` instead of `SUCCESS` (v1.0.5)
- [x] Fixed BSD/macOS `wc -l` leading-whitespace issue in `check_mailbox()` causing arithmetic syntax errors (v1.0.5)
- [x] Added default `*) : ;;` branch to all `case` statements missing it (`export_signatures.sh`, `import_ooo.sh`) (v1.0.5)
- [x] Eliminated command substitution masking in `export_calendar_resources.sh` and `export_dkim_keys.sh` heredocs (v1.0.5)
- [x] Updated `DOCNOTE.md` with Section 8: Perbaikan Kualitas Kode documenting all bugs, root causes, and fixes (v1.0.5)
- [x] Updated `CHANGELOG` with `### Fixed (Maintenance Pass)` section and refactored headings to Keep a Changelog standard (v1.0.5)

